{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WzfRDuFcrQjPCiALtU7AwG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd043-groups\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/groups: Print Group Memberships\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Shell scripts that check group-based permissions need a quick way to list a user's group\n6\t  memberships. The groups utility wraps the system group database into a one-line summary.\n7\t  The macOS BSD groups and GNU groups share the same basic behavior but differ in output\n8\t  formatting for named-user queries. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU\n9\t  reference binary (ggroups, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all argument\n10\t  combinations and edge cases, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n11\t\n12\tgoals:\n13\t  - G1: Print the group memberships of the current user when invoked with no arguments.\n14\t  - G2: Print the group memberships of one or more named users when USER arguments are given.\n15\t  - G3: Format output consistently with the GNU reference, including the \"user :\" prefix for named-user queries.\n16\t\n17\trequirements:\n18\t  R1:\n19\t    title: Default behavior\n20\t    items:\n21\t      - R1.1:\n22\t          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the group names of the current user, space-separated, on a single line followed by a newline, and exit 0.\n23\t      - R1.2:\n24\t          text: When invoked with one or more USER arguments, must print the groups for each user on a separate line and exit 0.\n25\t      - R1.3:\n26\t          text: If a named USER does not exist, must print an error message to stderr for that user and continue processing remaining users. Must exit 1 if any user was not found.\n27\t\n28\t  R2:\n29\t    title: Output format\n30\t    items:\n31\t      - R2.1:\n32\t          text: When no USER argument is given, must print only the space-separated group names with no prefix.\n33\t      - R2.2:\n34\t          text: \"When USER arguments are given, each line must be formatted as: 'user : group1 group2 ...' with the user name, a space, a colon, a space, and then the space-separated group names.\"\n35\t      - R2.3:\n36\t          text: Group names must appear in the order returned by the system group database.\n37\t\n38\t  R3:\n39\t    title: Differential testing\n40\t    items:\n41\t      - R3.1:\n42\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (ggroups) via pkg/testutils.\n43\t      - R3.2:\n44\t          text: \"Tests must cover: no-argument current-user output, single named user, multiple named users, nonexistent user error, and mixed valid/invalid users.\"\n45\t      - R3.3:\n46\t          text: Tests must verify the \"user :\" prefix format for named-user queries.\n47\t\n48\tnon_goals:\n49\t  - cmd/groups does not support any flags beyond --help and --version; it has no optional behavior modes.\n50\t  - cmd/groups does not print GIDs; only group names are output.\n51\t  - cmd/groups does not read user names from stdin; all input comes from command-line arguments.\n52\t\n53\tacceptance_criteria:\n54\t  - id: AC1\n55\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/groups with no arguments prints the current user's groups, matching ggroups.\"\n56\t    traces:\n57\t      - R1.1\n58\t      - R1.2\n59\t      - R1.3\n60\t  - id: AC2\n61\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/groups root prints 'root : ...' with root's groups, matching ggroups root.\"\n62\t    traces:\n63\t      - R1.1\n64\t      - R1.2\n65\t      - R1.3\n66\t  - id: AC3\n67\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/groups root nobody prints one line per user with the 'user :' prefix, matching ggroups.\"\n68\t    traces:\n69\t      - R1.1\n70\t      - R1.2\n71\t      - R1.3\n72\t  - id: AC4\n73\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/groups nonexistentuser exits 1 with an error message to stderr, matching ggroups.\"\n74\t    traces:\n75\t      - R1.1\n76\t      - R1.2\n77\t      - R1.3\n78\t      - R3.1\n79\t      - R3.2\n80\t  - id: AC5\n81\t    criterion: \"Differential test against ggroups passes for current-user, named users, and error cases.\"\n82\t    traces:\n83\t      - R1.3\n84\t      - R3.1\n85\t      - R3.2\n86\t  - id: AC6\n87\t    criterion: \"cmd/groups compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n88\t    traces:\n89\t      - R1.1\n90\t      - R1.2\n91\t      - R1.3\n92\t      - R2.1\n93\t      - R2.2\n94\t      - R2.3\n95\t      - R3.1\n96\t      - R3.2\n97\t      - R3.3\n98\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a40383e-f969-4fee-9010-160be781c594","uuid":"e163637b-7cbd-43f5-a9e6-83fa20387e8b","timestamp":"2026-05-20T14:11:19.318Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5363/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd043-groups.yaml","content":"id: srd043-groups\ntitle: \"cmd/groups: Print Group Memberships\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Shell scripts that check group-based permissions need a quick way to list a user's group\n  memberships. The groups utility wraps the system group database into a one-line summary.\n  The macOS BSD groups and GNU groups share the same basic behavior but differ in output\n  formatting for named-user queries. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU\n  reference binary (ggroups, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all argument\n  combinations and edge cases, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Print the group memberships of the current user when invoked with no arguments.\n  - G2: Print the group memberships of one or more named users when USER arguments are given.\n  - G3: Format output consistently with the GNU reference, including the \"user :\" prefix for named-user queries.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the group names of the current user, space-separated, on a single line followed by a newline, and exit 0.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: When invoked with one or more USER arguments, must print the groups for each user on a separate line and exit 0.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: If a named USER does not exist, must print an error message to stderr for that user and continue processing remaining users. Must exit 1 if any user was not found.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Output format\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: When no USER argument is given, must print only the space-separated group names with no prefix.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"When USER arguments are given, each line must be formatted as: 'user : group1 group2 ...' with the user name, a space, a colon, a space, and then the space-separated group names.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Group names must appear in the order returned by the system group database.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (ggroups) via pkg/testutils.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: no-argument current-user output, single named user, multiple named users, nonexistent user error, and mixed valid/invalid users.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Tests must verify the \"user :\" prefix format for named-user queries.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/groups does not support any flags beyond --help and --version; it has no optional behavior modes.\n  - cmd/groups does not print GIDs; only group names are output.\n  - cmd/groups does not read user names from stdin; all input comes from command-line arguments.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/groups with no arguments prints the current user's groups, matching ggroups.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/groups root prints 'root : ...' with root's groups, matching ggroups root.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/groups root nobody prints one line per user with the 'user :' prefix, matching ggroups.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/groups nonexistentuser exits 1 with an error message to stderr, matching ggroups.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"Differential test against ggroups passes for current-user, named users, and error cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"cmd/groups compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":98,"startLine":1,"totalLines":98}}}
